<spell-notebook "feed theming">
	<header level="1">
		Feed
		<header>A feed presents user activity chronologically.</>
	</>
	<feed-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-feed-*` tokens: set one on the feed, on any ancestor (`:root` for every feed), or on
			its box through `::part(feed)`. Its events inherit them.

			- Style an event's pieces with `::part()`: `event`, `label`, `image` and `icon`.
			- The feed's content parts also read a few tokens that are unset by default, so they are not in the table:
			  `--ui-feed-summary-color`, `--ui-feed-author-color` (a linked author; default the link colour),
			  `--ui-feed-date-color`, `--ui-feed-meta-color`, `--ui-feed-meta-action-color`, `--ui-feed-extra-color` and
			  `--ui-feed-extra-text-width` (default `500px`).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-feed {
			  --ui-feed-label-width: 3em;
			  --ui-feed-connected-color: var(--ui-primary);
			  --ui-feed-date-color: var(--ui-text-muted);
			}
			ui-event::part(label) {
			  filter: grayscale(1);
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`connected`, `ordered`, `divided` and the `basic` look reach the events as private switches (`--_feed-connected` ...);
				use the attributes, never set the `--_*` names. `color` (on the feed or one event) colours the number circles
				and the connecting line through `--ui-color`.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-feed" playground>
				<ui-feed>
					<ui-event image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22200%22 height=%22200%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
						<ui-content>
							<ui-summary><ui-author link="#elliot-fu">Elliot Fu</> added you as a friend <ui-date>1 Hour Ago</></>
							<ui-meta>
								<a href="#elliot-fu-likes"><ui-icon name="heart"></> 4 Likes</>
							</>
						</>
					</>
					<ui-event image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22200%22 height=%22200%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
						<ui-content>
							<ui-summary><ui-author link="#helen-troy">Helen Troy</> added 2 new illustrations <ui-date>4 days ago</></>
							<ui-extra text>Ours is a life of constant reruns. We're always circling back to where we'd we started.</>
							<ui-meta>
								<a href="#helen-troy-likes"><ui-icon name="heart"></> 1 Like</>
							</>
						</>
					</>
					<ui-event image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22200%22 height=%22200%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
						<ui-content>
							<ui-summary><ui-author link="#jenny-hess">Jenny Hess</> added you as a friend <ui-date>2 Days Ago</></>
							<ui-meta>
								<a href="#jenny-hess-likes"><ui-icon name="heart"></> 8 Likes</>
							</>
						</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
